    "story": "The flag is small enough to disappear inside her fist, and she waves it anyway, because the whole village has been waiting for somebody to start. The soldier does not wave back — his rifle is in both hands, and his job is to make sure the waving never has to stop. But he hears her. Somewhere behind his careful face, he is counting this moment as the first good one in a long string of hard ones, and he is glad she got to be the one who began it.",
