    "story": "The grass is soft under him in a way that makes him wonder how long it has been since he sat down on anything that was not a truck bed or a hard chair. His boots are caked with the dust of the morning's march, and the metal pot at his feet is empty now, and the tent behind him smells of canvas and rope and the rain that has not come yet. He is not asleep. He is not awake, exactly, either. He is in the in-between that a soldier learns to love: nobody shouting, nothing to carry, the whole afternoon his own until the moment it is not.",
