    "story": "The dirt on their faces is not makeup. It is the ground itself, kicked up by boots and by the men who came before them, and it sits in the lines of the older man's smile the way a man's history sits in his face — earned, and not washed off at the end of the day. He wears his glasses under a helmet that has seen a field or two, and he is grinning at the camera because someone has just said something worth laughing at, or because the day has been long and a grin is the cheapest thing a man can spend. Around him the boys in the same helmets are waiting for the word, rifles in hand, and the word is coming.",
