    "story": "The pencil never stops, not in this heat. She has a list of names on that board and a line beside each one, and the sun is already high enough that the paper throws the light back into her eyes, sunglasses or not. Somewhere behind her, somebody is laughing at a joke she did not hear, and she lets it go — the trucks will not wait for the joke, and neither will the day. She counts the names again, slower this time, because getting one wrong costs somebody a meal, a ride, a night of sleep. The canteen knocks against her hip with every step, and she keeps walking. The report will be finished before noon, and the names will all be accounted for.",
