    "story": "She types the order twice — once for the file, once for the man who will have to carry it out. The keys are stiff by now, the ribbon fading at the edges, and she has learned to hit the letters hard enough that the carbon copies stay legible all the way down to the third sheet. The mug beside her has gone cold, and she will drink it anyway, because the next page is already waiting in the tray and the officer who signs these things does not like to wait. Somewhere in the words she is copying is a place she has never seen and a morning she will not be there for. She keeps typing. The words are not hers, but the hands are.",
