    "story": "Yesterday she was somewhere else entirely — a kitchen, a classroom, a desk with a telephone that never stopped ringing — and now she sits in an afternoon that smells of dust and canvas, waiting for whatever comes next. The dress is striped, the cap is peaked, and neither of them is what she would have chosen for herself a year ago. She has learned not to choose. Behind her a soldier holds a mug and talks to someone out of frame, and she listens with half an ear while her hands stay still in her lap. She is thinking about the letter she has not written yet, and about the words that will fit in it, because some things are too big for a page and some are too small to leave unsaid.",
