    "story": "He listens to the engine the way other men listen to the radio — for the note underneath the noise. The hood is hot against his arms, the grease is under his fingernails and will stay there through two washings, and the wrench has gone slick in his palm. Somewhere behind him, a driver is leaning on the fender and telling him it was running fine yesterday, and he does not answer, because it was not running fine yesterday — it was running the way a tired machine runs, one bad morning away from stopping altogether. He finds the loose lead, tightens it, and steps back. The engine catches, steadies, and settles into the sound it is supposed to make. Tomorrow it will carry men who will never know his name.",
