    "story": "The bag bumps against his chest with every step, a small, steady rhythm he has walked to for miles. Inside it is the mask, and inside the mask is the smell of rubber and canvas that he has come to know as well as his own breath. He has never had to wear it for real, and he hopes he never will, but it hangs there anyway, heavy as a promise he did not ask to make. The helmet sits low over his eyes, the mustache is new enough that he still touches it without thinking, and somewhere ahead the road turns toward whatever the day has in store. He keeps walking. The bag keeps its rhythm, and so does he.",
